Wang,Qipeng Guo,\nKai Chen,Biqing Qi,Bowen Zhou\nhttps://github.com/JetAstra/SDAR 2\nA Survey of Reinforcement Learning for Large Reasoning Models\nKaiyan Zhang, Yuxin Zuo, ... Yihao Liu, ... , Bowen Zhou\nPreprint\nhttps://huggingface.co/papers/2509.08827 2\nScale-Doc:\nScaling LLM-based Predicates over Enormous Documents\nHengrui Zhang*,Yulong Hui*,Yihao Liu, Huanchen Zhang\nUnder Submission\nhttps://github.com/Seurgul/ScaleDoc 2\nUnder Submission\nG-LeCo: A GPU-Accelerated Framework for High-Throughput Learned\nCompression\nYouyang Xia,Feng Zhang,Jiawei Guan,Yihao Liu, Huanchen Zhang,Xiaoyong Du\n* means equal contribution.\nProjects\nEmbryo: a high-performance distributed analytical database\nNow\n◦Main contributor to the Embryo database, developing the core logic of the execution engine and network\ncommunication between workers.\nA book-sharing website with a distributed database backend\n2021\n◦Built a book-sharing website with a distributed NoSQL database as its backend. The database uses Mon-\ngoDB, Mongos, Redis, and HDFS as building blocks.\nDistributed system (MIT 6.824)\n2022\n◦Built a fault-tolerant distributed key-value store with linearizability.\nDocking scoring function in Drug discovery\nrf vina enhance 2\n◦Introduced a new scoring function of docking, leveraging non-bonded interaction information and outper-\nYihao Liu - Page 2 of 3--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTetraJet-v2: Accurate NVFP4 Training for Large Language Models with Oscillation Suppression and Outlier Control (https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.27527)\nciteturn2154academia16 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Title: TetraJet-v2: Accurate NVFP4 Training for Large Language Models with Oscillation Suppression and Outlier ControlAuthors: Yuxiang Chen, Xiaoming Xu, Pengle Zhang, Michael Beyer, Martin Rapp, Jun Zhu, Jianfei Chen\nTitle: TetraJet-v2: Accurate NVFP4 Training for Large Language Models with Oscillation Suppression and Outlier Control\nAuthors: Yuxiang Chen, Xiaoming Xu, Pengle Zhang, Michael Beyer, Martin Rapp, Jun Zhu, Jianfei Chen\nDate: Fri Oct 31 14:57:16 2025\n\nLarge Language Models (LLMs) training is prohibitively expensive, driving interest in low-precision fully-quantized training (FQT). While novel 4-bit formats like NVFP4 offer substantial efficiency gains, achieving near-lossless training at such low precision remains challenging. We introduce TetraJet-v2, an end-to-end 4-bit FQT method that leverages NVFP4 for activations, weights, and gradients in all linear layers. We identify two critical issues hindering low-precision LLM training: weight oscillation and outliers. To address these, we propose: 1) an unbiased double-block quantization method for NVFP4 linear layers, 2) OsciReset, an algorithm to suppress weight oscillation, and 3) OutControl, an algorithm to retain outlier accuracy. TetraJet-v2 consistently outperforms prior FP4 training methods on pre-training LLMs across varying model sizes up to 370M and data sizes up to 200B tokens, reducing the performance gap to full-precision training by an average of 51.3%.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEBT-Policy: Energy Unlocks Emergent Physical Reasoning Capabilities — Lacuna (https://lacuna.tiptreesystems.com/work/ebt-policy-energy-unlocks-emergent-physical-reasoning-capabilities/wrk_357a2c5ac2cc7908310122d325d22d62)\nciteturn2154search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Travis Davies, Yiqi Huang, Alexi Gladstone, Yunxin Liu, Xiang Chen, Heng Ji, Huxian Liu, Luhui Hu ... Unlike Diffusion Policies that use a fixed number of steps, EBT-Policy employs a dynamic termination criterion.\n\n# EBT-Policy: Energy Unlocks Emergent Physical Reasoning Capabilities\n\nTravis Davies, Yiqi Huang, Alexi Gladstone, Yunxin Liu, Xiang Chen, Heng Ji, Huxian Liu, Luhui Hu\n\narXiv 2025 · DOI\n\n## Introduction\n\nIn the rapidly evolving field of robot learning, Diffusion Policies have established themselves as a powerful standard. By iteratively denoising random signals into valid action sequences, they have enabled robots to perform complex manipulations. However, this success comes with significant overhead: high computational costs (often requiring 50–100 inference steps), exposure bias where small errors accumulate, and a fundamental lack of \"physical reasoning\" or self-awareness regarding uncertainty.\n\nTo address these challenges, we introduce EBT-Policy, a scalable Energy-Based Transformer architecture. EBT-Policy moves away from generative denoising and instead treats policy learning as a direct energy minimization problem. This shift not only yields a 50x reduction in inference steps but also unlocks \"emergent\" physical reasoning capabilities, such as the ability to automatically retry tasks upon failure without explicit training.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInteract-RAG: 与语料库推理与交互，超越黑箱检索 | alphaXiv (https://www.alphaxiv.org/zh/abs/2510.27566)\nciteturn2154search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Yulong Hui ... Image: Interact-RAG 概述 图1：传统黑箱RAG范式与所提出的Interact-RAG范式之间的比较。\n\n# Interact-RAG: 与语料库推理与交互，超越黑箱检索\n\nImageTsinghua University Alibaba Cloud\n\nYH\n\nYulong Hui\n\nCC\n\nChao Chen\n\nZF\n\nZhihang Fu\n\nYL\n\nYihao Liu\n\nJY\n\nJieping YeHuanchen Zhang\n\n## Abstract\n\n检索增强生成（RAG）通过整合外部信息，显著增强了大型语言模型（LLMs）。然而，主流的代理式RAG方法受限于一个关键缺陷：它们将检索过程视为一个黑盒查询操作。这限制了代理的动作仅限于发出查询，阻碍了其处理复杂信息检索任务的能力。 为此，我们引入了Interact-RAG，这是一种新范式，它将LLM代理从一个被动的查询发出者提升为检索过程的主动操纵者。我们通过一个语料库交互引擎打破了这个黑盒，为代理配备了一套动作原语，用于对信息检索进行细粒度控制。为了进一步增强代理在整个RAG流程中的能力，我们首先开发了一个推理增强型工作流，该工作流既支持零样本执行，也支持交互轨迹的合成。--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEBT-Policy: Energy Unlocks Emergent Physical Reasoning Capabilities (https://www.znakschoola.ru/?_=%2Fpdf%2F2510.27545%23UE7DkG0PaBHZOakR54g1Wl8%3D)\nciteturn2154search17 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; EBT-Policy: Energy Unlocks Emergent Physical Reasoning CapabilitiesTravis Davies\nEBT-Policy: Energy Unlocks Emergent Physical Reasoning Capabilities\nTravis Davies\nZhiCheng AI\nYiqi Huang\nZhiCheng AI\nAlexi Gladstone\nUIUC\nYunxin Liu\nTsinghua University\nXiang Chen\nPeking University\nHeng Ji\nUIUC\nHuxian Liu\nZhiCheng AI\nLuhui Hu\nZhiCheng AI\nAbstract\nFigure 1. EBT-Policy Diagram. EBT-Policy functions through\nsearching for a low energy action trajectory in cartesian or joint\nspace (z) through energy minimization. Further experiments will\nalso be updated.\n1. Introduction\narXiv:2510.27545v1  [cs.RO]  31 Oct 2025\nImplicit policies parameterized by generative models,\nsuch as Diffusion Policy [5], have become the standard for\npolicy learning and Vision–Language–Action (VLA) mod-\nels [26] in robotics. However, these approaches often suf-\nfer from high computational cost, exposure bias, and un-\nstable inference dynamics, which lead to divergence un-\nder distribution shifts. Energy-Based Models (EBMs) [28]\naddress these issues by learning energy landscapes end-\nto-end and modeling equilibrium dynamics, offering im-\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nllm-paper-radar/paper-river/QuartetII-2601.22813.org at main · zhaolin-amd/llm-paper-radar · GitHub (https://github.com/zhaolin-amd/llm-paper-radar/blob/main/paper-river/QuartetII-2601.22813.org)\nciteturn2154search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week;   * *TetraJet-v2 (Chen)*：NVIDIA 配方还是有数值震荡，需要异常值控制和震荡抑制等稳定性补丁。\n## 2025 | NVIDIA NVFP4 配方 + TetraJet-v2 + FourOverSix: 在共识路径上加补丁\n\n### 它看到了什么问题\n\n  * *NVIDIA 大规模配方*：要把上面的 idea 工业化跑通 12B 模型 12T tokens。他们用方块 (square block) 量化、反向 RHT、部分层留高精度。但仍然依赖 element-wise SR。\n  * *TetraJet-v2 (Chen)*：NVIDIA 配方还是有数值震荡，需要异常值控制和震荡抑制等稳定性补丁。\n  * *FourOverSix (Cook)*：前向的 scale 该缩到 6 还是缩到 4？给每个 block 自适应地选，前向 MSE 大幅下降。\n\n### 它的解法\n\n各自打各自的补丁，但 *都在反向沿用 element-wise SR*。FourOverSix 只动了前向，没碰反向；TetraJet-v2 动的是数值稳定性，没碰 SR 的方差。\n\n### 为什么这招管用（以及哪里埋了新坑）\n\n前向越改越好，但 *和 BF16 的 gap 没消*。这就把矛盾推到了反向 —— 既然前向 MSE 已经压到很低，剩下的差距大概率出在反向梯度的方差上。\n\n这就是 Quartet II 接手的位置。\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n陈键飞 - Academic Connection Network (https://academiconnection.github.io/thu_tsail_faculty_network/thu_tsail_chenjianfei_network/)\nciteturn2154search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; 陈小雨（Xiaoyu Chen）是陈键飞指导的第一位博士后，于2022至2024年间在 TSAIL 课题组开展研究工作。 ... 他已参与多项关于大语言模型量化训练的工作，包括 TetraJet-v2（NVFP4 精度大模型训练，ICML 2026 Spotlight）、INT8 训练动态回退以及结构化剪枝等研究。\n席浩诚本科毕业后同样选择前往加州大学伯克利分校继续深造。陈键飞连续培养出两名赴伯克利读研的本科生，充分体现了其在本科科研指导方面的卓越能力。\n\n### 5. 陈小雨（博士后，陈键飞指导，2022—2024）\n\n陈小雨（Xiaoyu Chen）是陈键飞指导的第一位博士后，于2022至2024年间在 TSAIL 课题组开展研究工作。在陈键飞指导下，她参与了生成流模型、量化训练等多个方向的研究。作为陈键飞团队的首位出站博士后，她的经历标志着陈键飞研究组从独立建组初期到形成完整人才培养体系的过渡。目前她已出站并继续从事相关研究工作。\n\n### 6. 李秉睿（博士研究生，陈键飞指导）\n\n李秉睿（Bingrui Li）是陈键飞最早独立招收的博士生之一，自2022年起在陈键飞指导下攻读博士学位。作为建组初期的学生，他的研究方向涵盖高效深度学习的多个方面。他的存在体现了陈键飞课题组从2022年开始系统化培养博士生的起点。\n\n### 7. 王梓腾（博士研究生，陈键飞指导）\n\n王梓腾（Ziteng Wang）自2023年起在陈键飞指导下攻读博士学位。他在多个研究项目中担任重要角色，参与了 SLA（稀疏线性注意力，ICLR 2026）等核心工作，并在高效推理系统方向上有所贡献。他的研究体现了陈键飞团队从量化训练向高效推理系统方向的延伸。\n\n### 8. 张芃乐（博士研究生，陈键飞指导）\n\n张芃乐（Pengle Zhang）于2025年加入陈键飞课题组攻读博士学位，是团队中较新的成员。他已参与多项关于大语言模型量化训练的工作，包括 TetraJet-v2（NVFP4 精度大模型训练，ICML 2026 Spotlight）、INT8 训练动态回退以及结构化剪枝等研究。作为团队中快速成长的新生力量，他的研究方向集中在低精度训练这一陈键飞团队的核心领域。\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInteract-RAG: Interactive Retrieval Paradigm (https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/interact-rag)\nciteturn2154search7 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2 months ago; Crawled: 3 weeks ago; Interact-RAG therefore redefines retrieval as an interactive substrate that can be shaped, constrained, and combined during reasoning rather than merely queried (Hui et al., 31 Oct 2025). ... This retention rule is important because it constrains synthesis toward successful interaction patterns rather than generic tool-use traces (Hui et al., 31 Oct 2025).\n\n## 3. Reasoning-enhanced workflow\n\nInteract-RAG does not rely solely on end-to-end prompting of an action-capable agent. It first introduces a reasoning-enhanced modular workflow with three collaborative modules: a Global-Planner, an Adaptive-Reasoner, and an Executor. The Global-Planner decomposes the initial user query into a stepwise execution plan. The Adaptive-Reasoner examines the evolving task state, including prior actions, gathered documents, and the plan, and decides whether to proceed or to reflect and refine when retrieval has failed or stalled. The Executor converts the reasoner’s directive into concrete action primitives and, after all subtasks, produces the final answer (Hui et al., 31 Oct 2025).\n\nThe workflow serves two purposes. First, it supports stable zero-shot performance by separating planning, reflection, and execution. Second, it generates structured agent trajectories that can later be used as training data. Those trajectories contain states, reasoning thoughts, and action sequences, and are retained only when the final answer matches ground truth. This retention rule is important because it constrains synthesis toward successful interaction patterns rather than generic tool-use traces (Hui et al., 31 Oct 2025).\n\nThe modularity also sharpens the contrast with prior agentic RAG methods. Prompt-only agents often collapse planning and retrieval into a single autoregressive stream, which can obscure whether failure originates in decomposition, evidence acquisition, or answer synthesis. In Interact-RAG, the workflow makes that decomposition explicit. This suggests that the system’s contribution is as much about policy factorization as about tool design.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEBT-Policy: Energy Unlocks Emergent Physical Reasoning Capabilities: Analysis, Review & Summary | Paperium (https://paperium.net/article/en/13035/ebt-policy-energy-unlocks-emergent-physical-reasoning-capabilities-analysis-review-summary-paperium)\nciteturn2154search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 11 months ago; Crawled: last month; Travis Davies, Yiqi Huang, Alexi Gladstone, Yunxin Liu, Xiang Chen, Heng Ji, Huxian Liu, Luhui Hu ... EBT-Policy reframes trajectory generation by assigning per-trajectory energies and producing actions through iterative energy minimization, implemented via an EBT architecture.\n\n# In-Depth Analysis & Summary: EBT-Policy: Energy Unlocks Emergent Physical Reasoning Capabilities\n\nImage: Paperium\n\nTravis Davies, Yiqi Huang, Alexi Gladstone, Yunxin Liu, Xiang Chen, Heng Ji, Huxian Liu, Luhui Hu\n\n31 Oct 2025 • 3 min read 417\n\nImage: EBT-Policy: Energy Unlocks Emergent Physical Reasoning Capabilities\n\nAI-generated image, based on the article abstract\n\n## Quick Insight\n\n### Robots Learn Faster by Following an Energy Signal\n\nImagine a robot that picks its next move by reading a single number, instead of thinking through dozens of steps. That number, a kind of energy score, tells what actions look safe or likely to work — and the robot acts fast. The new approach called EBT-Policy helps robots behave better in new places, using less training and less thinking time, so they get things done more quickly. In some tasks it figures out what to do in only a couple of tries, thats much faster than older ways. It also can bounce back from a bad action without being retrained, a simple form of zero-shot recovery that surprises people. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nG2-Reader: Dual Evolving Graphs for Multimodal Document QA (https://www.znakschoola.ru/?_=%2Fpdf%2F2601.22055%23UE7DkG0PaBHZOakR54g1Wl8%3D)\nciteturn2154search18 [wordlim: 200] Published: 7 months ago; Hui, Y., Lu, Y., and Zhang, H. ... Interact-rag: Reason and interact with the corpus, beyond\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEBT-Policy: エネルギーが創発的な物理的推論能力を解き放つ | alphaXiv (https://www.alphaxiv.org/ja/ov